{"title":"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems\">2019 AMC 10A #18</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12A Problems\">2019 AMC 12A #11</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6(Cheese_and_answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6(Cheese and answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Risky)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Risky)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Also_Risky)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Also Risky)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(No_Modular_Arithmetic,_Solving_the_Quadratic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (No Modular Arithmetic, Solving the Quadratic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the repeating base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> representation of the (base-ten) fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c01fbc67f37ea7e9d653ca7bdc5a81b149fa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accdad507f69e05d5edf22370a7efa423ee49d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{23}_k = 0.232323..._k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/69736c0dad97fe800934341e3dd15a9501331ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 13 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can expand the fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/25166078daa09b120d2ef195d4cd1b3696f07afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{23}_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> as follows: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3ddd5f37e8ea1ea9bacba39c51936e99f98d54f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{23}_k = 2\\cdot k^{-1} + 3 \\cdot k^{-2} + 2 \\cdot k^{-3} + 3 \\cdot k^{-4} + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that this is equivalent to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de3f2df4de994ca42b8e04b79c72d320b9c58a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2( k^{-1} + k^{-3} + k^{-5} + ... ) + 3 (k^{-2} + k^{-4} + k^{-6} + \\cdots )\\]\" width=\"406\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By summing the geometric series and simplifying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61baab88f88e280c09e4e114c20cf0a10a03eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2k+3}{k^2-1} = \\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />. Solving this quadratic equation (or simply testing the answer choices) yields the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/8890d1843f86f20a4711e45593b4dad9e0094020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"100\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764b81b942230a20855e999bc3c892881fbbc93f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0.2323\\dots_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d951455682b9261a789520061bc6d7465f510fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2a=23.2323\\dots_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>From this, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/7493ce553072d7eb83ed70a710b3ac09fd96f18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2a-a=23_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32314dcd06aa9ac02ae166ace9c498f0518d60f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{23_k}{k^2-1} = \\frac{2k+3}{k^2-1} = \\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"210\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Now, similar to in Solution 1, we can either test if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/599d2c8baf99c8703253d7ccd03e2842d87ec64c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with the answer choices, or actually solve the quadratic, so that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just as in Solution 1, we arrive at the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba71703f6aa9bbf745681822c9ca12b8f8e6f439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2k+3}{k^2-1}=\\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore now, we can rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/9004a40be8a073402d587eab4cdbe85ba95b0e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2k+3}{(k-1)(k+1)}=\\frac{7}{51}=\\frac{7}{3\\cdot 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"228\" height=\"42\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900aca5b9bb75ad101006c1ec6badbae16833509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+3=2(k+1)+1=2(k-1)+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"290\" height=\"18\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a prime number, we therefore must have that one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now, checking each of the answer choices, this will lead us to the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assuming you are familiar with the rules for basic repeating decimals, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a705278f6a0af91183875a5ae4e7c3da0b4b04b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.232323... = \\frac{23}{99}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />. Now we want our base, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, to conform to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e93d1016ec8b999553a60eab708341a56571bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23\\equiv7\\pmod k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb841943c0d832f45b5330512619ed03b184db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99\\equiv51\\pmod k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, the reason being that we wish to convert the number from base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Given the first equation, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> must equal 9, 16, 23, or generally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d70be966baaf9a9271c77e8a53e447c6ed5ca1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />. The only number in this set that is one of the multiple choices is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. When we test this on the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb841943c0d832f45b5330512619ed03b184db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99\\equiv51\\pmod k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, it comes to be true. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the LHS equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edcec3167c3184966b232292fee98e0ca421cea6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigg(\\frac{2}{k} + \\frac{2}{k^3} + \\cdots \\bigg) + \\bigg(\\frac{3}{k^2} + \\frac{3}{k^4} + \\cdots \\bigg) = \\frac{\\frac{2}{k}}{1 - \\frac{1}{k^2}} + \\frac{\\frac{3}{k^2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{k^2}} = \\frac{2k+3}{k^2-1},\\]\" width=\"522\" height=\"47\" /> from which we see our equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37369a222166fc6f32db16652a51411f4eb7e72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2k+3}{k^2-1} = \\frac{7}{51}, \\ \\ \\implies \\ \\ 51(2k+3) = 7(k^2-1).\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> therefore divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989181fa60643f4cdb41800fea8f6ebd8d883341.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 - 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> but as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is prime this therefore implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a3308b2b35ac19238cdacb19d452697e79d9b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k \\equiv \\pm 1 \\pmod{17}.\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> (Warning: This would not be necessarily true if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> were composite.) Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20bc985c2d1c4c1f4eb5a6f7eabfb653df63a348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} 16 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" /> is the only answer choice congruent satisfying this modular congruence, thus completing the problem. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~ Professor-Mom\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6.28Cheese_and_answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6(Cheese_and_answer_choices)\">Solution 6(Cheese and answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6(Cheese and answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can find that we just estimate the first two digits and can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/e/b2e765f417008c14f424118e82e6ce2283b685b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{k} + \\frac{2}{k^2} = \\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> and plug in some values and expand into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa7801d9309003f8d38d8c6af033e00f6e29882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2k+2}{k^2} = \\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"39\" /> and plugin some values and find that for 16, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f4296b78dee9e8064a7eb2144a528566e8dfe234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{34}{256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"38\" /> is very close to our target of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c01fbc67f37ea7e9d653ca7bdc5a81b149fa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ catattackskeyboard\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Risky.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Risky)\">Solution 7 (Risky)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Risky)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The fraction \\( 23/99 = 0.23232323... \\)\n</p><p>We have the base representation of \\( 7/51 \\).\n</p><p>There exists some fraction \\( a/b \\) such that \\( 7/51 \\cdot a/b = 23/99 \\).\n</p><p>\\( a = 23/7 \\), \\( b = 99/51 \\). Our fraction is then \\( a/b = (23/7) / (99/51) \\Rightarrow (23 \\times 51) / (7 \\times 99) \\Rightarrow 1173/693 \\).\n</p><p>Bases must be a multiple of the square of a number. We see that \\( \\sqrt{1173} \\) is about 34 and \\( \\sqrt{693} \\) is about 26. We subtract to get a common square, which is \\( 34-26 = 8 \\).\n</p><p>Our answer must be a multiple of 8, and the only one is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Also_Risky.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Also_Risky)\">Solution 8 (Also Risky)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Also Risky)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice how \\( 23/99 = 0.232323232323\\ldots \\), but round it down to \\( 0.23 \\).\n\\( 7/51 \\) is around \\( 0.13 \\).\nWe then have \\( 0.23 - 0.13 = 0.1 \\).\n</p><p>Multiply by 1000 to get \\( 0.1 \\times 1000 = 100 \\).\n</p><p>The fraction is the base \\( k \\) number multiplied by another number divided by 100. The number that gets closest to the number 100 when multiplied by another number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6f66809be1add52e351bd651aedb1ad340b95d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28No_Modular_Arithmetic.2C_Solving_the_Quadratic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(No_Modular_Arithmetic,_Solving_the_Quadratic)\">Solution 9 (No Modular Arithmetic, Solving the Quadratic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (No Modular Arithmetic, Solving the Quadratic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e7852884204b6a91f8b1d15554e3af734066d14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.\\overline{23}_k=\\dfrac{23_k}{k^2-1}=\\dfrac{2\\times k^1+3\\times k^0}{k^2-1}=\\dfrac{2k+3}{k^2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"346\" height=\"42\" />, so our equation is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/7417c7356afc92b033e104313343c706248360df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac7{51}=\\dfrac{2k+3}{k^2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"103\" height=\"41\" />, so now let's solve!\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/5269a697dcc07b168ca6c46e56b0bdc5b94359eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     \\dfrac7{51}&amp;=\\dfrac{2k+3}{k^2-1}\\\\     7k^2-7&amp;=102k+153\\\\     7k^2-102k-160&amp;=0,\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"245\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p>and now let's solve this equation with the Quadratic Formula!\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b50b15c41b8191bdfd9840d6cd7a80079194bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}     k&amp;=\\dfrac{-(-102)\\pm\\sqrt{(-102)^2-4(7)(-160)}}{2\\times7}\\\\     k&amp;=\\dfrac{102\\pm\\sqrt{10404+4480}}{14}\\\\     k&amp;=\\dfrac{102\\pm\\sqrt{14884}}{14}\\\\     k&amp;=\\dfrac{102\\pm122}{14}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"319\" height=\"180\" />\n</p><p>and we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer, so we will take the plus and not the minus since the minus will produce a negative non-integer value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in this case. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37338a2cc53a4cc1c452b7e97d83c9bd7d1d390.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k=\\dfrac{102+122}{14}=\\dfrac{224}{14}=\\boxed{16}.\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SCGzEOOICr4?t=1110\">https://youtu.be/SCGzEOOICr4?t=1110</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3YhYGSneu70\">https://youtu.be/3YhYGSneu70</a>\n</p><p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/W5V1UF-vSDE\">https://youtu.be/W5V1UF-vSDE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A\">2019 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</